This is a placeholder, not a real config file.

Get the real one from the Firebase console:
  1. https://console.firebase.google.com → your SYMX Systems project
  2. Project settings (gear icon) → your Android app
    (package name: com.symxsystems.symx_systems_app)
  3. Download google-services.json
  4. Save it as android/app/google-services.json (same folder as this file,
     but WITHOUT the .example suffix)

It's gitignored — don't commit it. It's tied to your Firebase project but
isn't a secret the way the release keystore or a service account key is
(it's bundled inside the app itself and is visible to anyone who unzips
the .apk), so losing it isn't catastrophic — you can always re-download it
from the Firebase console.

Once it's in place, push notifications (Netradyne safety alerts) work in
release builds. Without it, the app still builds and runs fine — you just
won't get push notifications.
